.TH "RAPTOR-SENSITIVITY" 1 "2026-10" "RAPTOR Studio" "RAPTOR Studio Manual"
.SH NAME
raptor\-sensitivity \- which inputs the answer is most sensitive to
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBraptor sensitivity\fR [\-h] [\-\-top N] [\-n N] [\-\-metric FIELD] [\-\-seed N|new] [\-j N] [\-\-timeout DURATION] [\-\-progress {auto,bar,json,none}] [\-f {text,json}] MODEL
.SH DESCRIPTION
One\-at\-a\-time tornado: vary each candidate input at a low and a high value, run every variant with Base's seed, and rank the paired swings. This screens inputs; it cannot show interactions.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Options
.TP
\fB\-\-top\fR \fIN\fR
how many inputs to screen (default 10)
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-trials\fR \fIN\fR
runs per variant (default: the model's own)
.TP
\fB\-\-metric\fR \fIFIELD\fR
per\-run field to watch (default availability)
.TP
\fB\-\-seed\fR \fIN|new\fR
salt every random stream (default: the fixed seed 'raptor run' uses, so the numbers match a plain run)
.TP
\fB\-j\fR, \fB\-\-jobs\fR \fIN\fR
cores to run on (default 1). Any 2 or more give the same numbers; they differ, equally validly, from 1
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fIDURATION\fR
stop the study after DURATION, e.g. 90s, 10m (default 30m); what it measured by then is reported and marked partial
.TP
\fB\-\-progress\fR \fI{auto|bar|json|none}\fR
progress on stderr (auto: only on a terminal; json: one object per line; none, or \-q, for silence)
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fI{text|json}\fR
output format (default text)
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
The ten inputs that move availability most, widest swing first.
.RS
.nf
\fBraptor sensitivity pump.rbds \-\-top 10 \-n 300\fR
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBraptor\fR(1)
